  news:
  - after: 0
    text: Night Window 3 reopens after its last receptionist was "reassigned".
    when: []
  - after: 0
    text: 'LATTICE: humans in stolen bio-suits seen near the Tower. Citizens urged
      to report anyone who blinks.'
    when: []
  - after: 0
    text: Kesh to wear five colours this cycle. Moon-readers 80% excited.
    when: []
  - after: 1
    text: INVADER CAUGHT AT TOWER. New night receptionist "a natural", says Lattice.
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 1
    text: 'Unregistered being sighted on floor 14. Lattice: "An isolated incident.
      Stay 60% content."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 1
    text: Citizen detained in error at the Tower released "mostly unharmed".
    when:
    - wrongful
  - after: 1
    text: 'Lattice reminds citizens: humans blink. Do not blink.'
    when: []
  - after: 1
    text: 'Earth signal detected again. Lattice: "Nothing to worry about. Do not
      listen to it."'
    when: []
  - after: 1
    text: 'Spore-meal up 3%: "a temporary harvest wobble", says the Food Lattice.'
    when: []
  - after: 2
    text: Tower arrests rise. "The night window is our wall," says Supervisor Graav.
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 2
    text: Floor 9 cleaners report "a smell of sweat". Audit office sealed for the
      night.
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 2
    text: 'Family of wrongly arrested clerk asks: "Who checks the checkers?"'
    when:
    - wrongful
  - after: 2
    text: 'Forged IDs flood the markets. Lattice: "Read every name letter by letter."'
    when: []
  - after: 2
    text: Elder Sunnek of the Ammaru turns 300. Celebrations 70% muted.
    when: []
  - after: 2
    text: Kesh turned an "unusual" shade last night. Moon-readers "not concerned".
    when: []
  - after: 3
    text: Block 22 family taken in for a "routine gill inspection". Neighbours 90%
      relieved.
    when:
    - flag:reported-22b
  - after: 3
    text: Block 22 resident complains the Lattice "ignores perfectly good tips".
    when:
    - flag:protected-22b
  - after: 3
    text: Night Window 3 now catches more invaders than windows 1 and 2 combined.
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 3
    text: 'Invader seen laughing in a Tower lift. Lattice: "Do not laugh back."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 3
    text: 'LATTICE: There is no basement in the Lattice Tower. Please stop asking
      about the basement.'
    when: []
  - after: 3
    text: 'Humans can''t even write a date, says expert: "They put dots in it."'
    when: []
  - after: 3
    text: Moon-readers confirm Kesh "will be whatever colour it is".
    when: []
  - after: 4
    text: Invader-free week at the Tower! Where are the invaders now? "Processed,"
      says the Lattice.
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 4
    text: 'Human "refugees" reported in the Moss Deeps. Lattice: "There are no refugees.
      Only invaders."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 4
    text: From tomorrow, Ammaru visitors to the Tower need a blue clan stamp.
    when: []
  - after: 4
    text: Maintenance worker taken for questioning after humming "the basement song"
      in a lift.
    when: []
  - after: 4
    text: Breathing on glass is now "a civic duty", says the Lattice.
    when: []
  - after: 5
    text: Lattice medal shortlist includes "a certain night receptionist".
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 5
    text: Fake glow spots found in a Tower bin. "Someone is getting sloppy," says
      Graav.
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 5
    text: UV lamps now on sale to night staff. "Holograms don't lie."
    when: []
  - after: 5
    text: Forgers move on to printed holograms, warns the Lattice.
    when: []
  - after: 5
    text: Plo frill-crowns win the cycle's crest parade for the 9th time.
    when: []
  - after: 6
    text: 'Visitors left queuing at the Tower at 02:00. Lattice: "Come back tomorrow,
      60% earlier."'
    when:
    - sent-home
  - after: 6
    text: 'Lattice: invader numbers "stable". Basement numbers "not a thing".'
    when: []
  - after: 6
    text: Kesh to go dark for one night next cycle. Citizens told to "just know"
      its colour.
    when: []
  - after: 6
    text: Night Window 3 receptionist's record "under review".
    when: []
  - after: 7
    text: '"Repeat invader" caught at Tower in her second stolen suit. Lattice: "They
      always come back. So do we."'
    when:
    - flag:mira2:security
  - after: 7
    text: 'Vessi clan elder: "Being wanted is not the same as being guilty." Lattice:
      "Noted."'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 7
    text: Vessi clerk arrested at Tower "because of the bulletin" sues the Lattice.
      Case 0% likely to be heard.
    when:
    - wrongful
  - after: 7
    text: WANTED bulletins to continue "until the Vessi problem is solved". Vessi
      asked to stay 70% calm.
    when: []
  - after: 7
    text: Lift Repair worker Fenn released. "I'll never hum again," he says.
    when: []
  - after: 7
    text: 'Earth signal now heard on three frequencies. Lattice: "Static. Very organised
      static."'
    when: []
  - after: 8
    text: 'End-of-cycle figures: Night Window 3 "the Tower''s finest". Graav "cautiously
      20% pleased".'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 8
    text: End-of-cycle audit finds "irregularities" at Night Window 3. Review continues.
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 8
    text: Maintenance worker Duun taken from the Tower. Lifts "may hum unattended"
      this cycle.
    when:
    - flag:duun5:security
  - after: 8
    text: 'NEW CYCLE C413 begins. Lattice: "New cycle, same rules. More rules, actually."'
    when: []
  - after: 8
    text: 'Refugee camps reported beyond the Moss Deeps. Lattice: "Those are not
      camps. They are invaders sitting down."'
    when: []
  - after: 8
    text: 'Kesh goes dark tonight. Moon-readers: "Everyone just knows what colour
      it is. Don''t ask."'
    when: []
  - after: 9
    text: 'Night Window 3 starts the cycle "as it ended: efficiently", says Lattice.'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 9
    text: 'Earth signal decoded: "a list of names", says leaked memo. Lattice: "There
      is no memo."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 9
    text: Humans now "study our moods", warns Lattice. Citizens told to vary their
      percentages.
    when: []
  - after: 9
    text: Moss Deeps checkpoint opens. Queue reported "60% long".
    when: []
  - after: 9
    text: Ammaru elder Sunnek calls for "calm, and fewer arrests of the elderly".
    when: []
  - after: 10
    text: Elderly citizen with lid-reflex arrested at Tower "for blinking". Released,
      20% blinking.
    when:
    - wrongful
  - after: 10
    text: 'Blue threads spotted on cuffs across the Moss Deeps. Lattice: "A fashion.
      Ignore it."'
    when:
    - flag:courier1:letin
  - after: 10
    text: Service lift codes changed overnight "for routine reasons".
    when: []
  - after: 10
    text: 'Lattice store: gill-scopes in stock from tomorrow. "See what they''re
      hiding."'
    when: []
  - after: 10
    text: Kesh lantern makers report record orders ahead of Lantern Night.
    when: []
  - after: 11
    text: 'Plo suits "the invaders'' new favourite", says Lattice. Plo clan: "Flattered
      and furious."'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 11
    text: Plo clerk arrested on wanted bulletin. "I have had this frill since hatching,"
      she says.
    when:
    - wrongful
  - after: 11
    text: Gill-scope sales soar. Some citizens scope themselves "just to be sure".
    when: []
  - after: 11
    text: Audit office reopens "for audits only". Visitors told not to ask what is
      being audited.
    when: []
  - after: 11
    text: A child at Block 22 asks the Lattice why humans want to come here. The
      Lattice does not answer.
    when: []
  - after: 12
    text: 'Caught invader begs at Tower: "My planet is burning." Lattice: "Planets
      don''t burn. Stay 70% calm."'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 12
    text: 'Tower security report: "Fewer arrests than expected" at Night Window 3.
      Investigation "not necessary yet".'
    when:
    - hid
  - after: 12
    text: Pressure questioning "works", says Lattice. Complaints from citizens "also
      work", say citizens.
    when: []
  - after: 12
    text: The basement button has been removed from all Tower lifts. "There was never
      a button."
    when: []
  - after: 12
    text: Earth signal now plays a song. Lattice bans humming in public buildings.
    when: []
  - after: 13
    text: '"Repeat invader" finally caught at Tower after three attempts. Her name
      was not released.'
    when:
    - flag:mira3:security
  - after: 13
    text: Lantern Night lights every street in Kesh's colour. Nobody gets it wrong.
      Almost nobody.
    when: []
  - after: 13
    text: 'Records office reports a file "read without permission". File contents:
      "nothing important".'
    when: []
  - after: 13
    text: Clinic floor closed for "deep cleaning" after an Earth child was treated
      there in secret.
    when: []
  - after: 14
    text: New archive link "catches forgers in seconds", says Lattice. Forgers "now
      inventing better names".
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 14
    text: 'Invented citizen "Pell-Ruu Nobody" seen dining on floor 21. Lattice: "A
      typo."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 14
    text: Archive records now link every window in the Tower. "We know who you are,"
      says the Lattice. "Probably."
    when: []
  - after: 14
    text: Duun of Maintenance wins "Most Talkative Employee" for the ninth cycle
      running.
    when: []
  - after: 14
    text: Files going down to the archive "faster than ever". Up? "That's not a direction
      files go."
    when: []
  - after: 15
    text: Lattice inspector "accidentally arrested during a test". Window under review.
    when:
    - flag:inspector1:security
  - after: 15
    text: Windows pass surprise inspections "with distinction". One receptionist
      named "reliable".
    when:
    - flag:inspector1:letin
  - after: 15
    text: 'Ruu clan protests wanted bulletins: "Our stalks are not a disguise."'
    when: []
  - after: 15
    text: The Lattice confirms it does not send inspectors. Inspectors confirm they
      are not being sent.
    when: []
  - after: 15
    text: Refugee camp beyond the Moss Deeps "dispersed". Where to? "Elsewhere."
    when: []
  - after: 16
    text: '"Skilled invaders" now outnumber clumsy ones, says Lattice. "Our windows
      are better still."'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 16
    text: 4th-question licences sell out. "Three questions was always too few," admits
      Lattice.
    when: []
  - after: 16
    text: 'Earth signal changes: "It sounds like a lullaby," says a moon-reader,
      who has since resigned.'
    when: []
  - after: 16
    text: Crest parade route announced. Lift maintenance "suspended for the festivities".
    when: []
  - after: 17
    text: 'Parade night arrests: four humans "cheered too loudly".'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 17
    text: Humans seen dancing at the crest parade. "Badly," adds the Lattice.
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 17
    text: Plo frill-crowns win the parade for a 10th cycle. Ruu stalk-seers demand
      a recount.
    when: []
  - after: 17
    text: 'Cycle 413 ends. Lattice figures: "invaders down, invaders up, invaders
      stable".'
    when: []
  - after: 17
    text: A Tower lift was heard going down during the parade fireworks. "Fireworks,"
      says the Lattice.
    when: []
  - after: 18
    text: 'SABOTAGE on floor 9: audit records burned. Lattice blames "an Earth spy
      who got past a window".'
    when:
    - flag:kett1:letin
  - after: 18
    text: 'Earth spy caught at Tower carrying "devices". Lattice: "Proof they are
      all dangerous."'
    when:
    - flag:kett1:security
  - after: 18
    text: Not every human is a refugee, says Lattice. Not every refugee is human,
      says nobody.
    when: []
  - after: 18
    text: 'Ammaru clan outraged by wanted bulletin: "Three eyes, zero crimes."'
    when: []
  - after: 18
    text: The audit office is now closed "until the audit is audited".
    when: []
  - after: 19
    text: Arrests at the Tower reach a record. The basement is "at capacity", says
      a leaked memo. There is no memo.
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 19
    text: Rumours of "a quiet door" at the Tower spread through the Moss Deeps.
    when:
    - hid
  - after: 19
    text: Stamp rule moves to Plo visitors. Ammaru stamp-makers "30% relieved".
    when: []
  - after: 19
    text: 'Lattice: "There is no basement." Lift engineers: "There is definitely
      a basement."'
    when: []
  - after: 19
    text: Cycle 414 begins with three new rules and a fourth "to be announced".
    when: []
  - after: 20
    text: Human "face-copier" caught minutes after the real citizen passed. "Like
      looking in a bad mirror."
    when:
    - flag:twin2:security
  - after: 20
    text: 'Orr-Vessi Talm reports "another me" on floor 2. Lattice: "Are you sure
      it wasn''t you?"'
    when:
    - flag:twin2:letin
  - after: 20
    text: 'The real Orr-Vessi Talm arrested at the Tower. His copy was let in. Lattice:
      "A mix-up."'
    when:
    - flag:twin1:security
  - after: 20
    text: Face-copying forgers "the new threat". Citizens urged not to have common
      faces.
    when: []
  - after: 20
    text: Service shaft workers report "voices". Voices report nothing.
    when: []
  - after: 20
    text: The Clinic reopens. Earth child "returned to where she came from". Where?
      "Elsewhere."
    when: []
  - after: 21
    text: Woman with a stolen processing file arrested at the Tower. File returned
      "unread".
    when:
    - flag:mira4:security
  - after: 21
    text: 'Second inspector arrested at the same window. Graav: "No comment."'
    when:
    - flag:inspector2:security
  - after: 21
    text: Missing Records files "probably misfiled". Probably.
    when: []
  - after: 21
    text: Lattice confirms basement "does not exist and is fully staffed".
    when: []
  - after: 21
    text: 'Kesh glows an odd colour over the Moss Deeps. Moon-readers: "Smoke."'
    when: []
  - after: 22
    text: 'Curfew "a success": fewer appointments, more arrests per appointment.'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 22
    text: Families left queuing at the Tower at closing time. "Come back before midnight,"
      says Lattice.
    when:
    - sent-home
  - after: 22
    text: 'CURFEW: no appointments after midnight. Night-shift workers told to "get
      sick earlier".'
    when: []
  - after: 22
    text: Lattice Clinic offers free gill scans to all Tower staff. "Routine," it
      insists.
    when: []
  - after: 22
    text: 'Plo clan elder Pluvia: "The rules change faster than the moon."'
    when: []
  - after: 23
    text: 'Vessi-suited humans "everywhere", says Lattice. Vessi: "We are everywhere.
      We live here."'
    when:
    - invader
  - after: 23
    text: 'The Earth signal falls silent. Moon-readers: "That''s worse."'
    when: []
  - after: 23
    text: Maintenance logs "temporarily confiscated" across the Tower.
    when: []
  - after: 23
    text: Night Window staff to be "reviewed one by one" before the Grand Audit.
    when: []
  - after: 24
    text: Graav watched Night Window 3 from the gallery all night. "Educational,"
      he says.
    when:
    - suspected
  - after: 24
    text: Night Window 3 "exemplary" under supervision. Graav "almost smiles".
    when:
    - '!suspected'
  - after: 24
    text: Stamp rule moves to Vessi visitors. Vessi stamp-makers "90% busy".
    when: []
  - after: 24
    text: 'Lattice publishes list of "invader behaviours": blinking, laughing, hoping.'
    when: []
  - after: 24
    text: Grand Audit scheduled for the end of the cycle. "Every window. Every decision."
    when: []
  - after: 25
    text: Second face-copier caught. "The eyes in the photo," says a receptionist.
      "Always the eyes."
    when:
    - flag:twin4:security
  - after: 25
    text: Real citizen arrested as their own copy. "I have never been less myself,"
      says Dosk-Plo Phae.
    when:
    - flag:twin3:security
  - after: 25
    text: Forgers now copying faces "from the archive itself". Archive "looking into
      it".
    when: []
  - after: 25
    text: 'Refugees seen boarding a ship at the Moss Deeps. Ship destination: "anywhere
      but Earth".'
    when: []
  - after: 25
    text: 'The lift log of the Tower has gone missing. Lattice: "There was never
      a log."'
    when: []
  - after: 26
    text: Third inspector arrested at Night Window 3. The window is "a problem",
      says the Lattice.
    when:
    - flag:inspector3:security
  - after: 26
    text: Cycle 414 ends. The Lattice thanks every citizen for being 60% content.
    when: []
  - after: 26
    text: Graav seen carrying a lift log to the basement. "There is no basement,"
      he tells reporters.
    when: []
  - after: 26
    text: Audit and Housing closed. Residents of floor 21 "temporarily rehoused"
      downstairs.
    when: []
  - after: 27
    text: 'Lockdown night: arrests at the Tower "higher than ever, as planned".'
    when:
    - caught
  - after: 27
    text: 'LOCKDOWN: Audit and Records sealed. The Grand Auditor arrives tomorrow.'
    when: []
  - after: 27
    text: Stamp rule moves to Ruu visitors. "It's a lottery," says a stamp-maker.
    when: []
  - after: 27
    text: 'Rumour: the Grand Auditor will "personally test the windows".'
    when: []
  - after: 28
    text: GRAND AUDITOR ARRESTED AT NIGHT WINDOW 3. Released after 40 minutes. "A
      thorough window," he says, through his teeth.
    when:
    - flag:auditor1:security
  - after: 28
    text: Grand Auditor passes through the Tower "without incident". Windows "adequate".
    when:
    - flag:auditor1:letin
  - after: 28
    text: The Grand Audit begins in two nights. Every receptionist's record will
      be read aloud.
    when: []
  - after: 28
    text: Families queue for clinic passes before the Grand Audit lockdown.
    when: []
  - after: 28
    text: 'The Earth signal returns, one word repeated: "Please."'
    when: []
  - after: 29
    text: Tower receptionist calls security on own sibling. "Rules are rules," says
      Lattice, approvingly.
    when:
    - flag:sel1:security
  - after: 29
    text: 'TOMORROW: THE GRAND AUDIT. The Tower locks down at 02:00.'
    when: []
  - after: 29
    text: Every lift in the Tower freshly oiled. "Suspiciously quiet," says Graav.
    when: []
  - after: 29
    text: Moon-readers predict Kesh "will be decisive" tomorrow.
    when: []
  messages:
  - id: hearing-act3
    after: -1
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: "Three strikes in the Basement act. The hearing found your mistakes honest
      \u2014 this time. Fined 30 shards. I read your answer logs, Ilo. If I ever
      find a slip you ignored, the next hearing is your last."
    when:
    - hearing
    - act3
    choices: []
  - id: hearing
    after: -1
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: 'Three strikes this act. Disciplinary hearing held in your absence: fined
      30 shards. Your slate is clean. It will not be clean twice.'
    when:
    - hearing
    - '!act3'
    choices: []
  - id: clinic
    after: -1
    from: Lattice Clinic
    text: Your sibling Sel was admitted last night with gill fever. Sel is resting
      at home now. The 50-shard bill is due tonight.
    when:
    - sel-hospital
    choices: []
  - id: landlord-debt
    after: -1
    from: Landlord Mott
    text: You owe me rent, Receptionist. I am 0% patient. Pay, or the Lattice hears
      about it.
    when:
    - debt
    choices: []
  - id: intro-lattice
    after: 0
    from: Civic Lattice
    text: Welcome to the Lattice Tower, Receptionist Ilo. Report to Night Window
      3 at 20:00. You are paid per correct decision; errors are deducted. Glory to
      the Lattice.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: intro-sel
    after: 0
    from: Sel
    text: BIG NIGHT!! You're going to be the best window person ever. I'm 90% proud
      and 10% coughing. Don't worry about the coughing. Will you bring me a story
      about a weird visitor?
    when: []
    choices:
    - text: I promise. Get some sleep.
      reply: YES. 100% asleep. (Not really.)
      flag: promised-stories
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Work is work, Sel. Rules are rules.
      reply: ...okay. 60% okay.
      flag: rules-first
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: graav-1-good
    after: 1
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: A clean first night. Don't let it go to your crest.
    when:
    - perfect
    choices: []
  - id: graav-1
    after: 1
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Mistakes on your first night. Everyone makes them once. Make them once.
    when:
    - '!perfect'
    choices: []
  - id: sel-1
    after: 1
    from: Sel
    text: Did you see one?? A real human?? Tuvo at school says they have hair EVERYWHERE
      and five fingers on each hand. FIVE.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: landlord-1
    after: 1
    from: Landlord Mott
    text: Rent is due every night, Receptionist. The Lattice pays you; you pay me.
      Simple.
    when:
    - broke
    choices: []
  - id: sel-2-sick
    after: 2
    from: Sel
    text: I'm fine. I'm 40% fine. The cough is louder at night, but I can hide it
      under the pillow.
    when:
    - meds-missed
    choices: []
  - id: sel-2
    after: 2
    from: Sel
    text: The new medicine tastes like burnt glow-moss. I'm 70% better! Did anyone
      laugh at your jokes yet?
    when:
    - '!meds-missed'
    choices: []
  - id: graav-2
    after: 2
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You arrested a citizen. Their family filed a complaint with my office.
      Read the rulebook. Then read it again.
    when:
    - wrongful
    choices: []
  - id: neighbour-2
    after: 2
    from: Neighbour Vaun
    text: Receptionist. You work for the Lattice, yes? The family in 22-B never shows
      their gills. Never. I've been watching. Will you report them?
    when: []
    choices:
    - text: I'll pass it on to the Lattice.
      reply: Good. Someone has to.
      flag: reported-22b
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Leave them alone. Gills are private.
      reply: Hmph. On your crest be it.
      flag: protected-22b
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: sel-3-sick
    after: 3
    from: Sel
    text: Don't be mad. I fainted at school. The nurse says I need my medicine every
      night. Every night, Ilo.
    when:
    - sel-sick
    choices: []
  - id: sel-3
    after: 3
    from: Sel
    text: I drew you at your window! You're the one with the big important face.
      Graav is the grumpy cloud.
    when:
    - '!sel-sick'
    choices: []
  - id: graav-3
    after: 3
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Records is closed tomorrow. Make them breathe on the glass. Citizens leave
      it clear.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: w3-caught
    after: 4
    from: Unknown
    text: "You're good at spotting us. Do you know where they take the ones you catch?
      Look down, receptionist. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - caught
    choices:
    - text: Delete the message.
      reply: (The message is gone. The feeling isn't.)
      flag: w3-deleted
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: 'Reply: "Who is this?"'
      reply: "Someone who sat at Window 3 once. Like you. \u2014 W3"
      flag: w3-replied
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: w3-missed
    after: 4
    from: Unknown
    text: "Some of us walked right past you. Maybe you noticed, maybe you didn't.
      Either way: thank you. Look down, receptionist. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - '!caught'
    choices:
    - text: Delete the message.
      reply: (The message is gone. The feeling isn't.)
      flag: w3-deleted
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: 'Reply: "Who is this?"'
      reply: "Someone who sat at Window 3 once. Like you. \u2014 W3"
      flag: w3-replied
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: sel-4
    after: 4
    from: Sel
    text: A Lattice man came to school and asked if anyone's family blinks. Everyone
      laughed. I didn't laugh. Is that bad?
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-4
    after: 4
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: 'Your first week is done. Tomorrow the clan rule starts: Ammaru need a
      blue stamp. Know the clans better than they do.'
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-5
    after: 5
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Tomorrow the forgers start faking holograms. A UV lamp shows the fakes.
      The Lattice store sells them. I'd buy one.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-5
    after: 5
    from: Sel
    text: Is it true the humans' planet is dying? Tuvo says they come here because
      there's nowhere else. Tuvo says a lot of things.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-6
    after: 6
    from: Sel
    text: You came home late again. I saved you some spore-meal. It's 50% spore-meal
      and 50% my drawing of you.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-6-late
    after: 6
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You closed the window with visitors still queuing. They complain to me,
      not to you. Faster tomorrow.
    when:
    - sent-home
    choices: []
  - id: graav-6
    after: 6
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Tomorrow's bulletin names the Vessi. A wanted list is a hint, not a verdict.
      I've seen windows arrest a whole clan on a hint.
    when:
    - '!sent-home'
    choices: []
  - id: mira-note
    after: 7
    from: Unknown
    text: "A note under your door, in careful, square handwriting: \"Twice now. My
      brother was taken at your window before you came. His file is on 14. If you
      ever see the name SELK, think of me. \u2014 M.\""
    when:
    - flag:mira2:letin
    choices:
    - text: Burn the note.
      reply: '(The paper curls. The name stays with you: SELK.)'
      flag: mira-note-burned
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Keep it in the drawer.
      reply: (You fold it small. Sel's drawings hide it nicely.)
      flag: mira-note-kept
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: sel-7
    after: 7
    from: Sel
    text: Can I ask a weird thing? I peeked when you were asleep. You close your
      eyes when you sleep. Like, all the way. Tuvo says only humans do that. Tuvo's
      wrong, right?
    when: []
    choices:
    - text: Everyone does it, Sel. Go to sleep.
      reply: Okay. 70% okay.
      flag: 
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: What else have you noticed?
      reply: Your neck. The gill lines are too straight. Like someone drew them.
        I like them though!
      flag: clue-sleep
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: graav-7
    after: 7
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You arrested a real citizen because the bulletin said Vessi. The bulletin
      also says the sky is up. Think.
    when:
    - wrongful
    choices: []
  - id: landlord-7
    after: 7
    from: Landlord Mott
    text: The Lattice asks landlords about their tenants now. What they eat, when
      they sleep. I told them you're boring, Receptionist. Stay boring.
    when:
    - '!wrongful'
    choices: []
  - id: graav-8-good
    after: 8
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Your first cycle is done and your record is good. Good records get noticed
      upstairs. Some things upstairs are better not noticed. Keep it good anyway.
    when:
    - loyal
    choices: []
  - id: graav-8
    after: 8
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: "Your first cycle is done. Your record has\u2026 gaps. Humans walk through
      your window, and you don't call me. I'm writing that down."
    when:
    - '!loyal'
    choices: []
  - id: w3-contact
    after: 8
    from: Unknown
    text: "New cycle, receptionist. You've seen enough of us now to know we're not
      monsters. Some of us are running from a dying world. Some of us are not. Can
      we talk? \u2014 W3"
    when: []
    choices:
    - text: Report the message to the Lattice.
      reply: (A Lattice clerk thanks you. Your message is "filed".)
      flag: w3-reported
      loyalty: 2
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: '"I''m listening."'
      reply: "Good. Watch for a courier with a blue thread on their cuff. \u2014
        W3"
      flag: w3-listening
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Ignore it.
      reply: 
      flag: 
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: sel-8
    after: 8
    from: Sel
    text: New cycle! I'm 80% better and 100% bored. Can you bring home a story about
      a nice human? Is there such a thing?
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-9
    after: 9
    from: Sel
    text: Tuvo's family moved away. Overnight. The teacher said "reassigned". Tuvo's
      mum blinked a lot, I think. Was that why?
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-9
    after: 9
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You reported a contact from "Window 3". Good. Most windows don't. If they
      write again, tell me first.
    when:
    - flag:w3-reported
    choices: []
  - id: sel-10
    after: 10
    from: Sel
    text: "The gill-scope ads are everywhere. Should we get one for home? Just to
      check\u2026 you know. Nobody. Just to check."
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: w3-10
    after: 10
    from: Unknown
    text: "A courier came through your window tonight. Blue thread on the cuff. Whatever
      you did, we saw it. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - flag:w3-listening
    choices: []
  - id: sel-11
    after: 11
    from: Sel
    text: I'm 70% better! The medicine tastes like burnt moss AND old lanterns now.
      Progress.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: landlord-11
    after: 11
    from: Landlord Mott
    text: Rent goes up next cycle. Lattice says landlords must "verify tenants' gills".
      I'm not doing that. Rent still goes up.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: w3-silent-offer
    after: 12
    from: Unknown
    text: "There's a wire under your desk that isn't on any plan. Connect it and
      you'll have a button. Press it instead of calling security, and we take them
      somewhere safe. Nobody upstairs sees a thing. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - flag:w3-listening
    choices:
    - text: Wire it in.
      reply: "Then we're in this together. Press it only when you're sure. \u2014
        W3"
      flag: w3-silent
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 1
      shards: 0
    - text: No. I do my job.
      reply: "Then do it well. We'll still be here. \u2014 W3"
      flag: 
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: graav-12
    after: 12
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Rumours say someone is turning the night windows. If anyone offers you
      anything, you tell me.
    when:
    - '!flag:w3-listening'
    choices: []
  - id: sel-12
    after: 12
    from: Sel
    text: Can we go to Lantern Night tomorrow? Oh. You work. Can I go with Vaun's
      kids? They're 40% nice.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-13
    after: 13
    from: Sel
    text: I found a photo in the old drawer. A woman with ROUND eyes holding a baby,
      in a blanket with stars on it. Is that from your work?
    when: []
    choices:
    - text: Put it back, Sel. It's nothing.
      reply: Okay. It's back. (It's not nothing. She looks like you.)
      flag: 
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Let me see it.
      reply: On the back it says "Tower, C393. Keep her safe." Who's "her"? Who's
        the baby, Ilo?
      flag: clue-photo
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: mira-file
    after: 13
    from: Unknown
    text: "I found my brother's file on 14. And another one, filed right behind it.
      A baby left at this Tower, cycle 393. Adopted by an Ammaru family. The baby's
      name was ILO. \u2014 M."
    when:
    - flag:mira3:letin
    choices:
    - text: Burn it. It's a mistake.
      reply: (You burn it. You remember every word.)
      flag: 
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: '"What else did it say?"'
      reply: "\"Mother: unknown. Species: see attached.\" The attachment was missing.
        \u2014 M."
      flag: clue-file
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 1
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: graav-14
    after: 14
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You have the archive now. Use it. A name with no record is a person who
      doesn't exist. People who don't exist don't complain.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-14
    after: 14
    from: Sel
    text: Cough's back. Don't buy food for me tomorrow, buy medicine. I can eat spore-meal
      crumbs. I'm small.
    when:
    - sel-sick
    choices: []
  - id: sel-14-well
    after: 14
    from: Sel
    text: I went to Lantern Night! Everyone's lanterns were the same colour except
      one kid's. The guards took his family. Why do they care about lanterns?
    when:
    - '!sel-sick'
    choices: []
  - id: graav-15-inspector
    after: 15
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: You arrested my inspector. He blinked, yes. He had a pass, yes. Read. The.
      Pass. It's in your file now.
    when:
    - flag:inspector1:security
    choices: []
  - id: graav-15-good
    after: 15
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: 'My inspector says you read his pass. Officially, I don''t have inspectors.
      Unofficially: good.'
    when:
    - flag:inspector1:letin
    choices: []
  - id: sel-15
    after: 15
    from: Sel
    text: Vaun's kids say the blinking people go to the basement and become lanterns.
      That's not true, right? Right?
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: w3-16
    after: 16
    from: Unknown
    text: "You should know something about Window 3, receptionist. The one before
      you was human. So was the one before her. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - flag:w3-listening
    choices:
    - text: '"Why tell me this?"'
      reply: "Because you should ask who put you there, and why they never check
        your eyes. \u2014 W3"
      flag: clue-w3
      loyalty: 0
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
    - text: Delete it.
      reply: 
      flag: 
      loyalty: 1
      mercy: 0
      suspicion: 0
      shards: 0
  - id: sel-16
    after: 16
    from: Sel
    text: You got a 4th question licence? Ask Graav what's in the basement. Ask him
      four times.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-17
    after: 17
    from: Sel
    text: PARADE!!! The Plo won AGAIN. I cheered for the Ruu. Somebody has to.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-17
    after: 17
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Too many humans walk through your window, Ilo. Either you're careless or
      you're kind. The Lattice doesn't have a word for kind.
    when:
    - suspected
    choices: []
  - id: graav-17-ok
    after: 17
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: End of cycle. Your record holds. Next cycle the rules tighten, and so will
      I.
    when:
    - '!suspected'
    choices: []
  - id: graav-18-kett
    after: 18
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: The man you let in burned the audit office. A spy, not a refugee. Now do
      you see why we check?
    when:
    - flag:kett1:letin
    choices: []
  - id: w3-18
    after: 18
    from: Unknown
    text: "Not all of us are running from something. The one who burned floor 9 wasn't
      ours. We're sorry. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - flag:w3-listening
    choices: []
  - id: sel-18
    after: 18
    from: Sel
    text: New cycle! You look tired. Like 30% tired. I'm making you a lantern. It'll
      be whatever colour you want.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: graav-19
    after: 19
    from: Supervisor Graav
    text: Act three of your career, receptionist. From now on, a hearing isn't a
      fine. It's the end of you. Three strikes. Count them.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: sel-19
    after: 19
    from: Sel
    text: Do you ever wonder if we're the strange ones? Like, from the outside? Tuvo
      used to say that. Before.
    when: []
    choices: []
  - id: w3-20
    after: 20
    from: Unknown
    text: "We know what's downstairs now. Processing. The people you report go down
      in the service lift, and they don't come back up. \u2014 W3"
    when:
    - flag:w3-silent
    choices:
    - text: '"I need proof."'
      reply: "Then get it. Someone in the Tower keeps a log of every trip down. \u2014
        W3"
      flag: w3-proof
      loyalty: 0
